.SS "int32_t schultz_node_set_fills_viewport (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, int32_t fills)"

.PP
Makes a node take its size from the window\&. A dialog covers the whole window, and so would any other full screen layer\&. Such a node is not placed by a parent, so nothing tells it when the window changed size and it keeps whatever size it had when it was shown\&. The window changes size more often than it looks: a phone being turned, a keyboard arriving, a band appearing across the top of the screen\&.
.PP
With this set, layout gives the node the viewport, so it follows the window without anything having to remember to tell it\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP The node to configure\&. 
.br
\fIfills\fP Nonzero to track the window, zero to be placed normally\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

