.SS "int32_t schultz_widget_paint_tree (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list, \fBschultz_arena\fP * arena, \fBschultz_rect\fP dirty)"

.PP
Walks the tree and emits every widget's drawing\&. Depth first, parents before children, so a child paints over its parent\&. Three tests decide whether a node is visited: it is skipped along with its subtree when it is not visible, and when its bounds do not touch the dirty rectangle\&. A node that clips pushes a clip that is popped on the way out\&.
.PP
Culling against the dirty rectangle is what keeps a one pixel change from rebuilding the whole command list\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to paint\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIlist\fP The command list to append to\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarena\fP Per frame scratch for widgets that need it\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIdirty\fP The region being repainted, in window coordinates\&. An empty rectangle means paint everything, which is what the first frame and a full repaint want\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for a NULL pointer, or a widget's own error, which stops the walk\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_widget_paint_tree_parts (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list, \fBschultz_arena\fP * arena, const \fBschultz_rect\fP * dirty, uint32_t parts)"

.PP
Paints a tree into a list, culled against several areas at once\&. What a frame driver uses\&. A frame usually has a few separate things that changed rather than one, and the rectangle covering all of them can be most of the window while what actually changed is a fraction of it\&. Naming each area separately is what keeps a small change small; docs/repainting\&.md has the measurements\&.
.PP
One walk whatever the count, because the walk costs the same whether it is testing one rectangle or eight, and doing it once per area would throw away most of what this is for\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to paint\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIlist\fP The list to append to\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarena\fP Per frame scratch\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIdirty\fP The areas that changed, or NULL for all of it\&. 
.br
\fIparts\fP How many, or zero for all of it\&. Above SCHULTZ_TREE_DIRTY_PARTS the rest are ignored\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_widget_paint_subtree (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list, \fBschultz_arena\fP * arena, \fBschultz_rect\fP dirty)"

.PP
Walks one subtree and emits its widgets' drawing\&. The same walk, started somewhere other than the root, which is what rendering one widget on its own needs\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to walk\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP The node to start at\&. Its own painting is included\&. 
.br
\fIlist\fP Where the commands go\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarena\fP Per frame scratch\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIdirty\fP The region being repainted\&. Empty means paint everything\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for a NULL pointer, or a widget's own error, which stops the walk\&. 
.RE
.PP

